  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary purpose of this project is to deliver immediate humanitarian and protection assistance to 64,700 conflict affected women, girls, boys, and men, particularly those living in informal shelters in Northern (contingent on access restrictions) and Middle areas (Deir Al Balah, Khan Younis) of Gaza. The project will target the most vulnerable IDPs according to economic and vulnerability criteria and in coordination with UN OCHA to avoid potential duplication. Oxfam has longstanding presence in Gaza and presently with23 staff in Gaza (3 of them in North Gaza). The project is proposing to partner with Palestinian Agricultural Relief Committees (PARC- established in 1983) and Juzoor for Health &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Social Development (established in 1996), both with significant experience working with Oxfam and in the proposed sectors/location of intervention. Jointly with local partners, Oxfam has since October 2023, supported over 262,424 individuals so far with immediate humanitarian assistance: water trucking, water production and sanitation, multi-purpose cash assistance, the distribution of blankets, sleeping mats, food parcels, hygiene, first-aid and female kits and more. As part of its overall response plan, Oxfam aims to reach 1,3 million people in the next 2 years.</narrative>
  </description>
